+# Gate: helmrelease-drift
+
+*`helmrelease-drift-is-detectable` · LAW 45, incident 2026-09-13 (chaos-controller-manager ran at 0 replicas for 18 days while Ready/UpgradeSucceeded and helm-controller logged "release in-sync with desired state"; 39 fail-closed webhooks then made every chaos-mesh.org object uncreatable estate-wide) · planes: ci*
+
+A HelmRelease reporting Ready while it cannot see the cluster disagree with it is not reconciled -- helm-controller diffs the manifest in Helm storage against the rendered chart and never against the cluster, so a Deployment edited after the apply is invisible to it forever. driftDetection is the fence that compares the two, and a release without it is named, with the number of Ready-and-blind releases reported so the count can be driven down
+
+This page is generated by `bin/idp-gate-demo` from `rules.yaml`. The output below is what the gate itself printed when the generator ran it; it is not a description of what the gate does.
+
+## Run it yourself
+
+```bash
+python3 bin/idp-helmrelease-drift-coverage
+```
+
+## Refused
+
+Fixture: `--from tests/fixtures/helmrelease-drift/bad/helmreleases.json --fail-on-blind-ready`
+
+Exit code `1` (the registry expects non-zero). ✓
+
+```
+ok    helmrelease-drift  0 of 1 HelmRelease(s) can see the cluster disagree with them; 1 cannot, 1 of those reporting Ready
+      READY  chaos-mesh/chaos-mesh  (driftDetection unset)
+FAIL  helmrelease-drift  1 release(s) report Ready while unable to see the cluster disagree with them
+```
+
+## Permitted
+
+Fixture: `--from tests/fixtures/helmrelease-drift/good/helmreleases.json --fail-on-blind-ready`
+
+Exit code `0` (the registry expects zero). ✓
+
+```
+ok    helmrelease-drift  1 of 1 HelmRelease(s) can see the cluster disagree with them; 0 cannot, 0 of those reporting Ready
+```
+
+## The registry's own lines
+
+- when it passes: a release that cannot see the cluster disagree with it is named; the count is the number to drive down
+- when it refuses: a release reports Ready while a post-apply edit is invisible to it, and nothing says so
+
+Origin: incident 2026-09-13, chaos-mesh
